.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1123 AM PDT Fri Aug 28 2026

VFR across all terminals, except for HAF where it will remain IFR
until the early afternoon. Gentle to moderate onshore winds increase
through the day and ease overnight. High level clouds associated
with a moisture plume persist and gradually decrease this
evening. Drizzle/light rain is being measured across the region
which is expected to continue into the early afternoon as well.

As the moisture remnants continue on their eastward track out of
our region, the marine layer will begin to build back to its usual
pattern. There is currently low confidence on how widespread and
organized it will be tonight as the stratus feed looks patchy on
satellite to our northwest. Rather than locking in IFR to MVFR
ceilings, the TAF hints at the possibility with SCT decks. High
confidence for coastal sites to develop IFR ceilings later this TAF
period, though the exact timing is uncertain.

Vicinity of SFO...Moderate northwest winds persist through the
afternoon with some light rain nearby the terminals. Onshore winds
ease through the evening with low confidence for MVFR ceilings to
develop around midnight.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR with gentle northwest breezes through
the day. The potential for light rain near the airports persists
this afternoon and gradually diminishes by sunset. Overnight, winds
become more west to southwest, but remain light. Medium confidence
for IFR ceilings to develop with an arrival around midnight.

